  "fact_notes": [
    "人物・出来事・制度は架空の教材例。実在の調査・統計・実証結果や医療基準ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "In a fictional school, five students volunteered to prepare a short musical performance for a community celebration planned for the end of the term.",
          "ja": "架空の学校で五人の生徒が学期末に予定された地域の祭典の短い音楽公演の準備に志願した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They concentrated on choosing music and practicing their movements together during the afternoon.",
          "ja": "午後に音楽選びと動きの練習に集中した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Nobody explicitly accepted responsibility for collecting equipment or communicating with the organizers about changes to the schedule.",
          "ja": "誰も機材収集や日程変更について主催者と連絡する責任を明示的に引き受けなかった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Ren completed these tasks whenever he noticed they had been neglected by the rest of the group.",
          "ja": "レンは他のメンバーが作業を放置していると気づくたびに済ませた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "As the celebration approached, the others assumed Ren would continue to manage all practical arrangements for the event.",
          "ja": "祭典が近づくと他の生徒はレンが引き続き行事の実務全般を管理すると想定した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "He gradually became frustrated because additional duties reduced his available rehearsal time.",
          "ja": "追加業務で練習時間が減り徐々にいら立った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "However, he hesitated to complain since nobody had directly requested most of this work.",
          "ja": "しかし誰も大半の仕事を直接頼んでいなかったため不満を述べるのをためらった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Their pattern of cooperation had developed without any discussion of the distribution of responsibilities among the members.",
          "ja": "メンバー間の責任の配分を一度も話し合わず協力のパターンが生じていた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "During the next meeting, Ren listed the tasks necessary before each rehearsal could begin.",
          "ja": "次の会合でレンは毎回の練習前に必要な作業を列挙した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "His classmates were surprised by the amount of preparation occurring outside scheduled sessions.",
          "ja": "級友は予定時間外の準備量に驚いた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They agreed to rotate ordinary duties and assign specific responsibilities after every meeting.",
          "ja": "通常業務を交代で行い毎回具体的担当を割り当てることにした。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They also identified urgent decisions that could not be postponed without affecting the project.",
          "ja": "延期すると活動に影響する緊急の判断も特定した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The revised arrangement did not make everyone's contribution identical, since certain duties required particular skills.",
          "ja": "特定の業務には技能が必要なので新案ですべての貢献が同じにはならなかった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Nevertheless, it provided a clearer basis for discussing expectations and requesting assistance when a difficulty arose.",
          "ja": "それでも期待を話し合い困難が生じたとき援助を求める明確な基盤ができた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Ren remained willing to help with unexpected difficulties.",
          "ja": "レンは予想外の困難にも進んで協力した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "His willingness was no longer interpreted as an unlimited commitment.",
          "ja": "その意欲が無制限の約束と解釈されなくなった。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Apparently successful cooperation can conceal an uneven distribution of effort.",
          "ja": "一見成功した協力は努力の不均等な配分を隠し得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A group benefits from identifying necessary work that is rarely visible to all of its members.",
          "ja": "全メンバーの目に触れにくい必要な仕事を特定することは集団の利益になる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Clear responsibilities preserve the value of spontaneous assistance while preventing it from becoming an unquestioned obligation.",
          "ja": "明確な責任は自発的援助の価値を守り当然視される義務になるのを防ぐ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "For these students, cooperation improved when they recognized preparation as an essential contribution.",
          "ja": "準備を不可欠な貢献として認識すると協力が改善した。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
